ens if the user presses hotkeys like `Alt+Z`.\n\n\n**Clarifying Opacity Controls**\n\nMy current concern centers on the interaction of WPF's `Window.Opacity` with Win32 window transparency. I've realized that with `WindowStyle=\"None\"` and `AllowsTransparency=\"False\"`, WPF's `Opacity` property doesn't affect the underlying Win32 window's opacity. I'm focused on the role of `WindowManager.SetTransparency` within this context, where I'm setting the actual Win32 window's transparency using `SetLayeredWindowAttributes`. Specifically I'm going to look at how `EnableTransparencyStyle()` effects the Win32 window.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"c:\\Users\\Arthur Henrique\\Documents\\GitHub\\Spectra\\src-csharp\\Platform\\WindowManager.cs","EndLine":75,"StartLine":40,"toolAction":"Viewing EnableTransparencyStyle in WindowManager.cs","toolSummary":"View EnableTransparencyStyle"}}]}
